{#
  Item provenance — objects carry history from their journey across players.

  When examining, identifying, or appraising an item, the narrator can
  reference its cross-player history. A sword might have "dried blood
  from a battle you weren't part of" or a key might "feel warm, as if
  recently held by someone else."
#}

{% if currentThing and currentThing.name %}
{% set history = getItemHistory(currentThing.name) %}
{% if history and history.length > 0 %}
<itemProvenance>
This item has a history beyond what the current player knows:
{% for entry in history %}
  <historyEntry>{{ entry.summary }}</historyEntry>
{% endfor %}
When describing this item, you may hint at its history through physical details: wear patterns, residual warmth, faint smells, scratches or marks. Do NOT explain the history directly — let the player infer it. The item "remembers" in texture, not words.
</itemProvenance>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
